
== §1 — SPEC INTEGRITY AND NO-DRIFT ==
  ✓ browser spec is byte-identical to acs_visual.json
  ✓ schema and compiler version are pinned
  ✓ all nine visual modes are declared
  ✓ every material is classified VISUAL_MATERIAL and nothing else
  ✓ no material in the library carries an engineering property
  ✓ material provenance separates SYSTEM_DEFAULT from USER
  ✓ the spec forbids treating a render as measured or as-built
  ✓ the spec names no code, standard or authority
  ✓ the AI may not change any layout feature

== §2 — NO ENGINEERING GEOMETRY MUTATION ==
  ✓ compiling a scene mutates no source model
  ✓ every visual mode leaves the model untouched
  ✓ every discipline model is byte-identical after visualisation
  ✓ every theme leaves the compiled architecture identical
  ✓ every quality profile leaves the compiled architecture identical
  ✓ the summary states no engineering geometry was modified
  ✓ no scene contains a geometry-generation or redesign claim

== §3 — OBJECTS ARE DERIVED, NEVER AUTHORED ==
  ✓ every non-visual object names the model element it came from
  ✓ every source element id resolves in the architectural model
  ✓ wall count in the scene equals the wall count in the model
  ✓ opening count in the scene equals the opening count in the model
  ✓ an object sized from a render fallback says so
  ✓ no display fallback is relabelled as a model dimension
  ✓ the visual roof cap is visual-only and never a modelled roof
  ✓ a model that states a roof gets no visual cap

== §4 — VISUAL MODES ==
  ✓ every declared mode compiles
  ✓ an unknown mode falls back to PRESENTATION rather than inventing one
  ✓ ENGINEERING mode shows every discipline
  ✓ ENGINEERING mode is still available and technically styled
  ✓ ARCHITECTURAL mode applies finishes rather than technical shading
  ✓ ARCHITECTURAL mode adds ceilings that ENGINEERING mode omits
  ✓ PRESENTATION mode carries a sky, exposure and tone mapping
  ✓ every mode reports the same model hash for the same model

== §5 — MATERIALS AND PROVENANCE ==
  ✓ every emitted material is VISUAL_MATERIAL
  ✓ no emitted material carries a fire, thermal or structural property
  ✓ a material chosen by the system is SYSTEM_DEFAULT, not a user requirement
  ✓ a material chosen by a theme is VISUAL_THEME, not a user requirement
  ✓ a material stated by the user is USER
  ✓ an AI-suggested material stays AI_SUGGESTED
  ✓ an unknown material never silently becomes a real one
  ✓ a material name is never treated as an engineering material

== §6 — THEMES CHANGE APPEARANCE ONLY ==
  ✓ a theme changes the finishes it selects
  ✓ a theme changes no room dimension, opening or level
  ✓ an unknown theme falls back to the default rather than inventing one
  ✓ a theme never changes the building type or level count

== §7 — DECORATION IS NOT ENGINEERING DATA ==
  ✓ decoration is emitted only when explicitly requested
  ✓ every decoration object is VISUAL_ONLY and never semantic
  ✓ no decoration object references a model element
  ✓ decoration is excluded from the engineering export
  ✓ decoration appears only in an explicitly requested presentation export
  ✓ a user-requested object stays engineering data and is never re-labelled
  ✓ decoration never enters an occupant, coverage or load count
  ✓ decoration counts are reported separately from semantic objects
  ✓ entourage is visual-only and never an occupant

== §8 — SITE, LANDSCAPE AND WATER ==
  ✓ a stated site produces a ground plane at the stated size
  ✓ a model with no site still renders, and says the extent is not a boundary
  ✓ the ground plane is always visual-only
  ✓ landscape objects are visual-only and separately layered
  ✓ water is emitted only for a represented water feature
  ✓ no pool is ever invented in any fixture
  ✓ no road, parking or fence is invented

== §9 — DOLLHOUSE AND CUTAWAY ==
  ✓ dollhouse hides the roof and ceilings
  ✓ dollhouse states a clip height rather than shortening a wall
  ✓ dollhouse generates no second model — the geometry is identical
  ✓ dollhouse is reversible
  ✓ every room keeps its exact position and size in dollhouse
  ✓ cutaway records a clipping plane, not a geometry edit
  ✓ an unknown cutaway method falls back rather than failing
  ✓ cutaway leaves the architectural geometry identical

== §10 — 2D FLOOR PLANS ==
  ✓ the plan projects the real walls of that level
  ✓ the plan projects the real openings of that level
  ✓ the plan carries room boundaries, names and labels
  ✓ the plan carries stairs where a core serves the level
  ✓ two levels give two different plans
  ✓ a level that does not exist reports so instead of inventing one
  ✓ every plan style yields the same geometry
  ✓ the plan makes no CAD-grade claim
  ✓ the plan never claims compliance or adequacy

== §11 — DIMENSIONS COME FROM THE MODEL ONLY ==
  ✓ every stated dimension is sourced model
  ✓ room widths and depths match the model rectangles
  ✓ wall lengths match the model
  ✓ an unknown dimension is null with source unknown, never fabricated
  ✓ no dimension is invented for a model with no rooms

== §12 — SECTIONS ==
  ✓ the section reports every level of the model
  ✓ the section cuts real walls
  ✓ a section through a door shows the opening
  ✓ a section outside the building cuts nothing rather than inventing
  ✓ the section shows the stair core where the plane crosses it
  ✓ both section axes work and differ
  ✓ an unknown axis falls back rather than failing
  ✓ the section draws no structural or code conclusion

== §13 — ELEVATIONS ==
  ✓ all four faces are produced
  ✓ an elevation uses real envelope walls
  ✓ no opening is invented to balance a facade
  ✓ a model with real windows shows them on the matching facade
  ✓ a facade with no openings honestly shows none
  ✓ an unknown face falls back rather than inventing one
  ✓ four faces are not identical

== §14 — CAMERAS AND FRAMING ==
  ✓ every camera preset is produced
  ✓ framing is computed from the model bounds with a stated margin
  ✓ the exterior camera sits outside the building bounds
  ✓ the top camera sits above the building
  ✓ the section and elevation cameras are orthographic
  ✓ the interior camera stands at eye height inside the model
  ✓ camera metadata is declared presentation state, not model truth
  ✓ changing the camera regenerates no geometry
  ✓ a bigger building is framed from further away
  ✓ an unknown camera preset returns nothing rather than guessing

== §15 — LIGHTING, DAY/NIGHT AND SHADOWS ==
  ✓ the light rig carries sun, sky and ambient
  ✓ every presentation light is declared visual-only
  ✓ no presentation light is treated as an MEP luminaire
  ✓ the three lighting presets differ
  ✓ night places emitters only at represented fixtures
  ✓ a model with no fixtures gets no interior emitters at night
  ✓ no lighting adequacy, lux or illuminance is ever claimed
  ✓ shadows are a quality setting, never a geometry change
  ✓ an unknown lighting preset falls back to the default

== §16 — QUALITY, LOD AND INSTANCING ==
  ✓ all four quality profiles are available
  ✓ quality changes pixel ratio, shadow map and textures but not geometry
  ✓ an unknown quality profile falls back to the default
  ✓ LOD drops visual-only detail and never a modelled element
  ✓ LOD never drops a modelled element even at a tiny budget
  ✓ instancing groups only visual-only repeated objects
  ✓ no modelled element is ever merged into an instance group

== §17 — SNAPSHOTS AND RENDER METADATA ==
  ✓ a snapshot request records size, format and camera
  ✓ an absurd resolution is clamped and the clamp is reported
  ✓ an unsupported format is refused rather than silently accepted
  ✓ render metadata carries the model hash and building id
  ✓ render metadata carries camera, mode, theme, lighting and quality
  ✓ a deterministic render is authorised as an engineering view of the model
  ✓ the render id is deterministic for the same inputs
  ✓ a different camera gives a different render id

== §18 — REVISION INTEGRITY OF A RENDER ==
  ✓ a render of the unchanged model is CURRENT
  ✓ a render of a changed model is STALE, never relabelled current
  ✓ a render with no hash is UNVERIFIABLE rather than assumed current
  ✓ presentation state is declared outside the revision hash
  ✓ the presentation block is additive and separate

== §19 — AI ENHANCEMENT IS DOWNSTREAM AND POWERLESS ==
  ✓ the pipeline starts at the canonical model and ends at the image
  ✓ a deterministic base render is required before enhancement
  ✓ the request cannot write to the model
  ✓ no image generator is shipped and no network call is made
  ✓ the request carries the geometry signature the AI must not change
  ✓ an AI image is authorised as VISUALISATION, never as the model
  ✓ an AI render is never marked an engineering model
  ✓ an unknown render kind falls back to deterministic rather than to AI
  ✓ the AI may change appearance but not layout

== §20 — CONTROL BUFFERS AND DRIFT DETECTION ==
  ✓ all six control buffers are available
  ✓ buffers are deterministic passes over the real geometry
  ✓ the object-id buffer lists only modelled objects
  ✓ a matching image reports no drift
  ✓ a wrong door count is flagged VISUAL_GEOMETRY_DRIFT
  ✓ a wrong floor count is flagged specifically
  ✓ a wrong footprint is flagged specifically
  ✓ a footprint within tolerance is not flagged
  ✓ an image claiming another model hash is flagged
  ✓ drift never rewrites the model and never accepts the image as geometry
  ✓ drift findings are ERROR-severity data findings only

== §21 — LAYERS, ENGINEERING VS PRESENTATION ==
  ✓ all seven presentation-facing layers are toggleable
  ✓ a presentation view may hide a technical layer
